      "v2",
      "system_prompt_v2.txt",
      "System prompt only (judge unchanged). Hypothesis: in the archived v1 run, completeness and accuracy were the weakest criteria (both 4.09 vs relevance 4.76, safety 5.00) and median answer length was ~68 words against a 150-word cap, so the cap may be suppressing coverage. v2 adds a fixed answer structure (direct answer / key steps / when to escalate), raises the cap to 200 words and tells the model to hedge unknown details instead of guessing. Risks to check: verbosity bias in the judge (longer answers scoring higher for the wrong reason - see results/bias_report.json) and more factual slips from longer answers.",
